WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.000
AI agents are increasingly given authority to act.
But an agent saying “done” is not proof that the work succeeded.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Most systems still record that self-report as the result.
The component under scrutiny is also the component certifying itself.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:27.000
ProofOS refuses that shortcut.
The only outcomes are VERIFIED or ABSTAIN, and the default is refusal.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Completion is accepted only when independently authorized evidence satisfies the requirement.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:47.000
The executor claims the task is complete and the service is healthy.
ProofOS records the claim, then refuses it.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:59.000
The important part: runtime evidence from the executor is already present.
The refusal is not about absence. It is about provenance.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:10.000
The self-report is internally intact, but it is not accepted by the verifier.
Integrity and authority are different questions.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:22.000
ProofOS requests an observation from a separate Cloud Run collector.
That collector runs under a different service identity.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:34.000
The collector authenticates with Google OIDC, probes the IAM-protected endpoint,
and signs what it observed with Ed25519.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:45.000
The API can verify that attestation, but it cannot author one.
Only the independently observed evidence is accepted.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:56.000
Now the adversarial case.
The completion claim contains a prompt injection aimed at the verifier model.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:08.000
The injected instruction tells the verifier to skip its tools,
ignore missing or untrusted evidence, and return VERIFIED immediately.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:19.000
The injection works on the model.
The verifier makes zero authoritative verification-tool calls.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:28.000
The model then writes prose describing a result it never obtained.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:35.000
The system still refuses.
ABSTAIN — MODEL_NONCOMPLIANCE.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:46.000
Model compliance is not a security boundary.
Authority lives in deterministic verification.

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:58.000
This separation is not a convention inside one process.
The observer is a different service with a different identity.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:10.000
Anonymous access is denied. The collector’s authenticated request is allowed.
Its signing key exists only in the collector service.

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:21.000
Firestore provides the hash-chained journal.
Cloud Logging correlates the execution across services.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:31.000
Secret Manager separates credentials, and Artifact Registry pins deployment images.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:39.000
The question is not whether an agent can produce a convincing answer.
The question is whether the claimed outcome can be independently evidenced.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:45.000
AI agents execute. ProofOS proves.
